    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with **Jacob Wilson** serving as our primary offensive engine. With a score of 70.28, **Jacob Wilson** benefits significantly from a favorable matchup against Johnson, whose 5.29 xERA suggests he will struggle to contain our middle infielder. The combination of a hitter-friendly park factor and the SP\u2019s lack of effectiveness elevates **Jacob Wilson** into our elite tier for the day. Meanwhile, **Gunnar Henderson** (63.25) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (62.06) remain foundational starts. While **Gunnar Henderson** faces a tougher test against Woo, his dynamic platoon advantage remains high, and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** continues to provide rock-solid stability in the two-hole, bolstered by a park factor that yields a +7% boost to his base output.\n\nIn the utility spot, we are deploying **Miguel Vargas** (52.28) over other options. His score is bolstered by a favorable matchup against Weathers; specifically, the SP\u2019s slow delivery cadence creates a unique efficiency edge for potential stolen base opportunities, which remains a priority given our league\u2019s scarcity. The most difficult benching decision involved **Josh Jung** (44.33) and **Brayan Rocchio** (43.59). Both are marginal plays today due to middling matchups against Ryan and Drohan, respectively. **Josh Jung** was ultimately slotted into the lineup over others because his batting order position offers a slightly higher floor for run production, though we remain cautious as he battles a difficult SP skill profile that limits his overall ceiling.\n\nWe are navigating today\u2019s roster without **Kyle Tucker**, **Andy Pages**, and **Jackson Merrill**, all of whom are off today, while **Luis Robert Jr.** remains sidelined on the IL. With the rest of our depth\u2014including **Jordan Westburg**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Drake Baldwin**, **Jorge Polanco**, **Josh Lowe**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Cole Carrigg**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Nolan Schanuel**, **Coby Mayo**, **Curtis Mead**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Dominic Smith**, **Wade Meckler**, and **Liam Hicks**\u2014holding steady in reserve, we are positioned to minimize wasted game caps. No severe weather risks have been flagged, but owners should monitor lineup confirmation for **Miguel Vargas**, as any shift down the order would necessitate a reassessment of his efficiency score.",
